# Round 10 (#400 re-cut, decided 1): the CLOSED, REVIEWED inert-member allowlists. A member
# access on a watched module expression is consumed ONLY when its literal name is a key in
# the module's table here: each entry names one member whose OWN use yields no read,
# launch or import capability, with a one-line reason. The member's VALUE can still
# reach a module (a Python-level function carries its module namespace in __globals__;
# round 11, decided 4), so the reflective dunders of a consumed value are judged at
# their own nodes on any base instead of being claimed absent here. EVERY
# other member is an unsupported-use FINDING at its line, pinned like any other (round 9
# consumed ANY non-watched member, and both round-9 reviews reproduced launchers and loaders
# passing through that consumption: subprocess.getoutput, importlib.util.find_spec,
# importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader, importlib.reload, os.fdopen and a literal getattr
# chain through os.path).
